      "message": "So I think we should not call free_page() here. (I\u0027m working on a counterpart upstream patch now).\n\nIf I\u0027m not mistaken, all we need is:\n\n```\nclear_slot_flag(zram, index, ZRAM_WB);\nzram_release_bdev_block(zram, get_slot_handle(zram, index));\nzram_set_handle(zram, index, handle);\n```\n\nIn exchange we can remove quite a lot of code from this function - all the flags/attrs restore, double atomic inc, ac-time thing, etc.\n\nBut more importantly, we don\u0027t restore all of the flags.  For instance, slot could have been INCOMPRESSIBLE and we lose that flag.  So after writeback/prefetch this slot will become recompression target again (but we might have already tried that and figured it was worthless).\n\nAm I missing something?",
